#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#. {ph2}: <code>SI</code>
#: website/public/showcase/th04/index.html:571
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:showcase/th04/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}01 · Read the bullet index.{ph1} The stack argument is loaded into {ph2}. In a "
"16-bullet ring, this member index runs from 0 through 15."
msgstr ""

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#. {ph2}: <code>SHL AX,8</code>
#. {ph3}: <code>IDIV</code>
#: website/public/showcase/th04/index.html:576
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:showcase/th04/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}02 · Space the directions around a full turn.{ph1} {ph2} multiplies by 256. The "
"count is zero-extended into a word, then {ph3} divides the product by that count. For "
"count 16, each index advances 16 angle units."
msgstr ""

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#. {ph2}: <code>AX</code>
#: website/public/showcase/th04/index.html:583
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:showcase/th04/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}03 · Add the player direction.{ph1} The two subtractions form player-minus-origin"
" coordinates. The direction helper returns an angle in {ph2}; adding it turns the "
"whole ring toward the player."
msgstr ""

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#. {ph2}: <code>ADD AL,[0x53ad]</code>
#: website/public/showcase/th04/index.html:589
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:showcase/th04/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}04 · Add the pattern's rotation.{ph1} {ph2} adds the template angle. Elly's "
"initial template sets it to zero; other patterns can use the same helper with a "
"rotation."
msgstr ""

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#. {ph2}: <code>AL</code>
#: website/public/showcase/th04/index.html:595
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:showcase/th04/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}05 · Keep the final angle in one byte.{ph1} The store writes {ph2} to the spawn-"
"angle field. Values wrap after 255, just as the unsigned-byte cast does. The "
"surrounding source also converts this angle and speed into velocity."
msgstr ""

